  data:
    partName: Frontal Lobes (Left & Right)
    scientificName: Lobi Frontales
    systemType: 5
    keyFunction: Largest cerebral lobes responsible for executive cognitive control, voluntary motor initiation, language expression, and personality.
    description: Contains primary motor cortex (precentral gyrus), premotor cortex, and Broca's motor speech area.
    clinicalFacts:
    - Coordinates complex decision making and emotional regulation.
    - Damaged in frontal lobe dementia or Phineas Gage-type traumatic injuries.
