  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HumanAnatomy.AnatomyPart
  data:
    partName: Right Median Nerve
    scientificName: Nervus Medianus Dexter
    systemType: 5
    keyFunction: "Major anterior peripheral nerve formed by union of lateral and medial cords (C5\u2013T1)."
    description: Descends medial to brachial artery; traverses cubital fossa and anterior forearm, passing beneath flexor retinaculum into carpal tunnel.
    clinicalFacts:
    - 'Motor: Forearm flexors, thenar muscles (thumb opposition), and lateral two lumbricals.'
    - Compression under flexor retinaculum causes Carpal Tunnel Syndrome (numbness in thumb, index, middle finger).
