  data:
    partName: Mandible (Lower Jaw)
    scientificName: Mandibula
    systemType: 1
    keyFunction: Strongest and largest bone of the human face; forms the lower jaw and articulates mastication.
    description: Articulates with temporal bones at bilateral temporomandibular joints (TMJ).
    clinicalFacts:
    - Possesses mental protuberance (chin) unique to Homo sapiens.
    - Anchors inferior dentition and major chewing musculature.
