    scientificName: Nervus Tibialis Dexter
    systemType: 5
    keyFunction: "Larger terminal branch of sciatic nerve (L4\u2013S3); courses through popliteal fossa down posterior leg."
    description: Passes posterior to medial malleolus through tarsal tunnel to divide into medial and lateral plantar nerves in foot.
    clinicalFacts:
    - 'Motor: Gastrocnemius, soleus, tibialis posterior, flexor digitorum longus, and intrinsic foot sole muscles.'
    - Tarsal tunnel syndrome causes burning sole and heel pain.
